<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">World Trade Organization</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1995</span> · Also known as WTO</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The World Trade Organization is an international body founded in 1995 to succeed the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade and regulate trade between its members. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s entry in 2001 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>'s in 2007 marked their integration into the world economy after decades of market reform.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/world-trade-organization.jpg" alt="World Trade Organization" width="320" height="163" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BlankMap-World6.svg: Happenstance et al / derivative work: Danlaycock · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WTO_members_and_observers.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
